            "review_title": "Review at Hoa Túc",
            "review_text": "1926yanks\nSeattle, Washington753 contributions\n0\nA Great Restaurant\nAug 2025 • Friends\nContemporary Vietnamese it is. I ate twice at the District 3 restaurant, relatively new. The more established one, in D1, is usually crowded. I was at this one twice on weekends, & it was surprisingly not crowded. So the vibe is more Chill & less trendy than the Established D1 one\nThe special beef cubes with greens was fantastic. The filet sea bass was excellent too. And the restaurant had a free dessert buffet, offered on weekends. \nThis restaurant should be more busy! It’s great. It always has a mix of Vietnamese & Westerners, a healthy sign. Great staff too.\nRead more\nWritten August 10, 2025",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-14",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
